        "description": "Over 4 billion years, Earth's atmosphere has been transformed from a composition devoid of molecular oxygen (O$_2$) to one where O$_2$ is now 21% of our modern atmosphere by volume. With high quantities of O$_2$, an ozone (O$_3$) layer can form and partially shield the surface from biologically harm",
        "title_cn": "臭氧层演变的模拟：对早期地球、系外行星和生命搜索的影响"
      },
      {
        "title": "Hybrid Reasoning Agents",
        "link": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.18861v1",
        "pubDate": "2026-10-13T17:59:31Z",
        "description": "How can we build an agent that thinks beyond human language, yet still acts through it in the external environment? Modern LLM agents still reason and interact through text, while latent reasoning offers an efficient internal medium but lacks native tool access and reasoning transparency. We bridge ",
        "title_cn": "混合推理代理"
      },
      {
        "title": "Visual Tokens on Demand: Visual Budgeting for Scalable and Efficient Multi-Image Reasoning in Multimodal LLMs",
        "link": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.18858v1",
        "pubDate": "2026-10-13T17:59:24Z",
        "description": "Multimodal large language models have advanced rapidly, but most remain optimized for single-image inputs. Multi-image reasoning is costly because each image adds many visual tokens, increasing encoding and attention demands. Existing techniques that address the above issue, including visual token p",
        "title_cn": "可视化按需令牌：多模式LLM中可扩展且高效的多图像推理的可视化预算"
      },
      {
        "title": "Exact Topological Compliance: Generating Persistence-Equivalent Graphs",
        "link": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.18856v1",
        "pubDate": "2026-10-13T17:59:19Z",
        "description": "Persistent homology summarizes the topological evolution of a graph as persistence diagrams (PDs). Generating graphs whose topology matches a target descriptor is increasingly important, yet existing topology-aware generative models rely on soft regularization, producing graphs whose PDs may only be",
        "title_cn": "精确拓扑符合性：生成持久性等效图"
      },
      {
        "title": "Interaction Latents as Actions for Contact-Rich Manipulation",
        "link": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.18855v1",
        "pubDate": "2026-10-13T17:59:16Z",
        "description": "Contact-rich manipulation requires robots to coordinate not only where to move, but also how contact and force should evolve throughout an interaction. Yet most robot policies represent actions primarily as motion trajectories, using tactile signals as inputs or auxiliary prediction targets without ",
        "title_cn": "交互潜伏期作为富接触操作的操作"
      },
      {
        "title": "ForceWAM: Decoupling Future and Response Learning from Demo and Play Data for Contact-Rich Manipulation",
        "link": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.18852v1",
        "pubDate": "2026-10-13T17:58:44Z",
        "description": "Expert demonstrations show how to complete contact-rich tasks, but provide limited coverage of how interaction forces respond to different actions. Task-agnostic play provides broader experience of contact dynamics without specifying task goals. To fully leverage these two types of data, we introduc",
        "title_cn": "ForceWAM ：从富接触操纵的演示和播放数据中解耦未来和响应学习"
      },
      {
        "title": "Contact Trajectory Prompting: In-Context Transfer of Contact-Rich Behaviors from a Single Demonstration",
        "link": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.18848v1",
        "pubDate": "2026-10-13T17:58:08Z",
        "description": "In-context robot learning enables robots to acquire new behaviors from demonstrations without test-time parameter updates. However, visual and kinematic specifications alone may not distinguish contact-rich behaviors that share similar motions but require different interaction intensities or pattern",
        "title_cn": "工单轨迹提示：来自单个演示的富工单行为的上下文转移"
      },
      {
        "title": "Seeing Double: The Theory Defying Twin Flares of TDE 2022dbl",
        "link": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.18840v1",
        "pubDate": "2026-10-13T17:56:56Z",
        "description": "Partial tidal disruption events, in which a star survives a close passage by a supermassive black hole and may be disrupted again on a subsequent encounter, provide a unique probe of supermassive black hole properties and accretion physics. We examine TDE 2022dbl, a partial tidal disruption event ca",
        "title_cn": "《Seeing Double: The Theory Defying Twin Flares of TDE 2022dbl》"
      },
      {
        "title": "Scaling Online Optimal Transport Minibatches for Flow Matching",
        "link": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.18838v1",
        "pubDate": "2026-10-13T17:56:26Z",
        "description": "A central challenge in scaling flow models is maintaining stability in training and integration. In flow matching, this stability depends critically on how source samples are paired with data. Independent random pairing introduces substantial stochasticity, motivating minibatch optimal transport (OT",
        "title_cn": "扩展在线优化运输迷你批次以实现流量匹配"
      },
      {
        "title": "Peering into the Midplane of the DM Tau Disk using N2H+ and DCO+",
        "link": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.18821v1",
        "pubDate": "2026-10-13T17:51:30Z",
        "description": "Planets form in the midplanes of protoplanetary disks, thus investigating the properties of the midplane region can shed light on the physical and chemical processes governing the evolution of planetary systems. In this work, we study the conditions near the midplane of the disk around DM Tau using ",
        "title_cn": "使用N2H +和DCO +对准DM Tau磁盘的中板"
      }
    ],
